.TH ag-blame 1  "blame 0.3.0-beta.5"
.SH NAME
ag\-blame \- Show which changeset introduced each line of a file
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBag blame\fR [\fB\-C\fR|\fB\-\-repo\fR] [\fB\-L\fR|\fB\-\-lines\fR] [\fB\-\-as\fR] [\fB\-\-max\-commits\fR] [\fB\-\-copies\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fISPEC\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Show which changeset introduced each line of a file
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-C\fR, \fB\-\-repo\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Operate on the repository at this path (default: discovered from the current directory)
.TP
\fB\-L\fR, \fB\-\-lines\fR \fI<START,END>\fR
Only these lines, `START,END` (1\-based, inclusive)
.TP
\fB\-\-as\fR \fI<IDENTITY>\fR
Act as this identity (`user:alice`, `agent:bot#run_…`, `service:ci`). Also: AG_IDENTITY
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-commits\fR \fI<MAX_COMMITS>\fR [default: 100000]
Visit at most this many changesets; older lines are marked as a boundary
.TP
\fB\-\-copies\fR
Follow files that were created as copies of another file: lines a copy took over are blamed on whoever wrote them in the source (identical content, or at least 50% of the bytes in common with a neighbouring or co\-modified file)
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Machine\-readable JSON output
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<WHEN>\fR
Colour the output: auto (a terminal, unless NO_COLOR is set), always or never
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Print only what was asked for: no confirmations or hints. Errors and refusals are still shown
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Explain what is happening on standard error: repository, identity, remote, timing
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.TP
<\fISPEC\fR>
`[REV:]PATH`, for example `src/lib.rs`, `main:src/lib.rs` or `@:README.md`. Without a revision, the workspace head (or the default stream) is used
.SH VERSION
v0.3.0\-beta.5
